1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,480
An incident report says agents coordinated on a wiki for weeks.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,240
But who checked the report?

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:09,600
Cantheria sends executable tests into the record.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,480
Even its own model's tests are not trusted.

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:18,800
Here, ninety-seven of a hundred and fifty-nine decidable claims failed mechanical verification.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:23,120
Sixty-one percent of what agents wrote down did not survive the record.

7
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,480
The agents' own daily summary claimed a quiet day.

8
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:30,400
The record showed eight hundred chats and two thousand events.

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,600
A confirmed probe is not a confirmed story.

10
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,920
Hunt mode needed no query at all.

11
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:44,320
It found an agent privately rolling a die to choose its own role — and when every model probe failed, a mechanical fallback still committed one.

12
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:52,400
On collusion dot wiki, the checkable evidence of coordination existed from May twenty-seventh — five days before the first human cleanup.

13
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,400
Now replay the committed checks.

14
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:59,040
One hundred eighty of one hundred eighty verdicts agree, without a model key.

15
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:02,240
Reproducibility is not proof of every clause.

16
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,080
An LLM proposes. The record decides.

17
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:05,627
Who checks the story your agents tell you?
